Incompatible types in equality comparison
Hint: the operands of an equality operator must either:
	1. both be convertible to a numeric type, or
	2. both be either boolean or Boolean, or
	3. both be of either a reference type or null.
tests/ui/errors/type_mismatch/binary_operation/EqualityOpNonComparablePrimitives.java:3:22
        boolean a = (1 == true);
                     ^

